  id: journal.mars_gravity
  title: "Heavier Than the Moon, Lighter Than Home"
  author: "Suit Tech M. Varga"
  dateLine: "Field note, Mars base zone"
  category: 5
  body: "Mars pulls at a bit under two-fifths of Earth gravity: more than the Moon, still light enough to catch you out on a jump. The dust haze also flattens distances, so trust your scanner over your eyes."
  placement: 2
  bodyId: body.sol.mars
